.TH BANDWIDTH-USAGE-REPORT 1 "2026-10-01" "bandwidth-usage-reporter 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bandwidth-usage-report \- generate a bandwidth usage report from vnStat exports
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bandwidth-usage-report
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bandwidth-usage-report
reads monthly and daily vnStat JSON or CSV exports, writes a normalized
bandwidth usage JSON file, scores that JSON with the packaged model, and renders
a one-page PostScript report. The report can also be sent to
.BR lpr (1)
when printing is explicitly enabled.
.PP
The supported executable is
.IR /usr/bin/bandwidth-usage-report .
The
.I /opt/bandwidth-usage-reporter
tree is an implementation detail containing the application scripts and
isolated Python runtime. The wrapper sets up that runtime before executing the
report script. Do not run the internal script in
.I /opt
directly as a normal interface. Calling it with the system Python interpreter
will not use the packaged NumPy/SciPy runtime and may fail unless dependencies
are installed separately. Receiver deployments should use
.BR bandwidth-usage-run-report (8),
normally via systemd.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--input-dir " DIR
Read vnStat exports from DIR. The default is
.IR /var/spool/bandwidth-usage .
.TP
.BI "--output-dir " DIR
Write generated JSON and PostScript output under DIR. The default is the input
directory.
.TP
.BI "--scorer " PATH
Use PATH as the scoring script. The default is
.I score_bandwidth_usage.py
next to the reporter script.
.TP
.BI "--date " DATE
Use an explicit report date. DATE may be
.I YYYY-MM-DD
or
.IR YYMMDD .
When omitted, the newest daily vnStat row supplies the report date.
.TP
.BI "--previous-months " COUNT
Include COUNT complete prior months before the current month-to-date series.
The default is 2.
.TP
.B --include-zero-days
Include current-month daily rows whose month-to-date total is zero.
.TP
.B --include-zero-months
Include prior monthly rows whose total is zero.
.TP
.BI "--json-out " PATH
Write the generated and scored JSON document to PATH instead of the default
output file name.
.TP
.BI "--ps-out " PATH
Write the rendered PostScript report to PATH instead of the default output file
name.
.TP
.B --print
Submit the rendered PostScript report to
.BR lpr (1).
.TP
.BI "--lpr-option " OPTION
Pass OPTION to
.BR lpr (1).
May be repeated.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.SH INPUT FILES
The reporter selects the newest matching monthly and daily file in the input
directory.
.PP
Monthly JSON patterns:
.IR monthly.vnstat.*.json ,
.IR monthly.vnstat.json .
.PP
Monthly CSV patterns:
.IR monthly.vnstat.*.csv ,
.IR monthly.vnstat.csv ,
.IR vnstat.monthly.csv .
.PP
Daily JSON patterns:
.IR daily.vnstat.*.json ,
.IR daily.vnstat.json .
.PP
Daily CSV patterns:
.IR daily.vnstat.*.csv ,
.IR daily.vnstat.csv ,
.IR vnstat.daily.csv .
.SH OUTPUT FILES
Unless overridden, output files are named with the report date:
.TP
.I bandwidth_usage.YYMMDD.json
Normalized and scored report data.
.TP
.I bandwidth_usage.YYMMDD.ps
Rendered one-page PostScript report.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B non-zero
Argument parsing, input parsing, scoring, rendering, file I/O, or printing
failed. Python tracebacks are written to standard error for unexpected failures.
.SH EXAMPLE
Generate output without printing:
.PP
.nf
bandwidth-usage-report \\
    --input-dir /var/spool/bandwidth-usage \\
    --output-dir /var/spool/bandwidth-usage/.cache \\
    --date 260525
.fi
.PP
Generate a sample report from packaged example data:
.PP
.nf
mkdir -p /tmp/bandwidth-usage-sample
bandwidth-usage-report \\
    --input-dir /usr/share/doc/bandwidth-usage-reporter/bw_sample_data/raw \\
    --output-dir /tmp/bandwidth-usage-sample \\
    --date 2026-08-31
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/bandwidth-usage-reporter/bw_sample_data/raw
Packaged sample vnStat input data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bandwidth-usage-run-report (8),
.BR lpr (1)
